From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211_hwsim: protect the Beacon frames in the
 driver

mac80211 adds the MME with the BIP MIC of the BIGTK inside
ieee80211_beacon_get(), so a field that the driver writes into the
Beacon frame afterwards breaks the MIC, and a station with the BIGTK
drops the frame. The fields that hwsim writes now, the Timestamp and
the Power Management bit, are masked out of the MIC, but the next patch
has hwsim count the AP Removal Timer in the Beacon frame.

Take the BIGTK of an AP interface as a hardware key, so that mac80211
leaves the protection to the driver, and protect each Beacon frame with
ieee80211_encrypt_tx_skb() just before it is sent, as for the group
addressed frames. The PN stays the one of mac80211's key. As for the
other keys of mac80211_hwsim, mac80211 then asks the driver for the
sequence number of the key and gets 0.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
@@ -2428,6 +2428,17 @@ static int mac80211_hwsim_set_key(struct
 	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_GCMP:
 	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_GCMP_256:
 		break;
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_AES_CMAC:
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_BIP_CMAC_256:
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_BIP_GMAC_128:
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_BIP_GMAC_256:
+		/* the BIGTK protects a Beacon frame only after the driver
+		 * changed it
+		 */
+		if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
+		    (key->keyidx == 6 || key->keyidx == 7))
+			return 0;
+		return 1;
 	default:
 		return 1;
 	}
@@ -3273,6 +3284,11 @@ static void __mac80211_hwsim_beacon_tx(s
 		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
 		return;
 	}
+
+	if (ieee80211_encrypt_tx_skb(skb) < 0) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	info = IEEE80211_SKB_CB(skb);
 	if (ieee80211_hw_check(hw, SUPPORTS_RC_TABLE))
